1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Hello, this is Hatomugi.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Today, I have this. Tada!
"Koubutsu Wokashi" (Mineral Candies).

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,500
I'll be eating kohakuto (crystal amber) candy called Koubutsu Wokashi.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,500
Together with the sweets, it came with this lovely postcard,

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:47,000
and this jewel-shaped message card that says "Happy Valentine." Isn't it cute?

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,500
Today is Valentine's Day. Did you all have a wonderful Valentine's Day?

7
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Now, let's open up the box right away.

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Open! Tada. Not visible quite yet.

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:25,500
By the way, this is the limited January–February edition called "Winter Fragments × Kakeru."

10
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,500
The flavors are written right here.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Now, let's remove this thin sheet of paper. Here we go... Tada! Still not visible!

12
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,500
Still keeping us waiting, isn't it?

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Alright, this time for real. Here we go... Open! Tada!

14
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,500
Wow, amazing! They really look like genuine gemstones. So pretty.

15
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:24,500
Look how they sparkle! I'm not sure if the camera captures the shine, but it's wonderful. And to think these are completely edible!

16
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:09,000
When lined up like this, they're so pretty. Sparkling just like real gemstones.

17
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:33,000
Now, I'll taste them one by one. Bon appétit / Itadakimasu.

18
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:06,500
How should I describe it... it has a sophisticated, mature sweetness.

19
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Next is this one. This one looks very mineral-like. Let's eat.

20
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:56,500
That one was probably white chocolate & rum raisin? I can taste the subtle difference. Having rum raisin in it definitely gives it an adult flavor.

21
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:03,500
This little pink one, maybe cassis? Let's eat.

22
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,500
Might be cassis.

23
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Peach coconut. Let's eat.

24
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Delicious, and the sound is so nice—very crunchy. It's refined and tastes like a gourmet sweet for adults.

25
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:58,000
I think this pairs wonderfully with tea. So, to accompany today's treat, I prepared some rooibos tea.

26
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:14,500
I've been really into rooibos tea lately. I bought a large bulk bag and brew a big pot of it.

27
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,000
What's this purple one... maybe raspberry? Let's eat.

28
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Delicious.

29
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,500
Yellow is caramel.

30
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:59,500
Brown is cocoa & orange peel.

31
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:36,500
I love this one so much. Cocoa & orange peel go so well together. I thought it was an unusual combination, but the slight bitterness of cocoa blended with refreshing orange is amazing.

32
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Next is black. Black is black sesame. Black sesame.

33
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:11,000
The black sesame tastes intensely of black sesame! The rich flavor really surprised me. It's very tasty.

34
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:26,500
Did I introduce all of them? For purple, earlier I mentioned raspberry, but there's also grape. My tastebuds might not be distinguishing them well... this might be grape. Let's eat.

35
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:57,000
I couldn't quite tell. The purple ones like grape or raspberry have a subtle sweetness, so with my dull palate, I couldn't tell them apart.

36
00:08:57,500 --> 00:09:07,500
There is only one green piece, so it feels almost a waste to eat, but green is La France pear. Let's eat.

37
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:48,500
This one I can clearly tell: it's La France pear flavor. Delicious. Overall, as I said earlier, it has an elegant and mature flavor. A very luxurious taste.

38
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:56,500
From here on, I'll quietly focus on eating. Please enjoy the chewing sounds.

39
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:20,500
Eating a bigger piece completely fills your mouth, creating an interesting texture. Pure bliss.

40
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:32,500
May I pop a whole mouthful in? It might not be the most polite, but...

41
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:36,000
I'll try mixing various flavors together.

42
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,500
Pure bliss.

43
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Delicious.

44
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,000
There are only a few left now.

45
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:02,500
I'll eat the small ones.

46
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:19,500
Only 3 left. I saved three big ones for the end.

47
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:33,000
This one is so gorgeous. I feel like saving it for the very last. Let's eat the black one first. Black sesame. Let's eat.

48
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:22,500
Delicious.

49
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:30,500
Now for this crimson one, a mineral candy resembling a bright red ruby. Let's eat.

50
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:29,000
The final piece. This one has gold leaf on top and glitters so beautifully. Such intricate craftsmanship. It almost feels a waste to eat, but here goes the last one. Where should I bite? I'll take a big bite.

51
00:24:58,500 --> 00:25:04,500
So much volume. One last bite. Let's eat.

52
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:31,500
Thank you for the meal (Gochisousama deshita). Finished it completely! It was delicious.

53
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:43,000
Honestly, there were quite a lot of pieces, so I thought about saving the rest for later, but it disappeared in an instant!

54
00:25:43,500 --> 00:26:01,000
Of course it's a sweet confection, but it's not an overwhelmingly intense sweetness. It has such an elegant sweetness that I just kept snacking away. It was so delicious.

55
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:12,000
If you're curious about Koubutsu Wokashi, definitely look them up. Looking at their lineup, they release different variations for each season.

56
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:24,000
While this January–February limited box is no longer sold, they already announced a March limited edition. All of them looked so cute.

57
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:35,000
I love how the colors and flavors change with the seasons. If I have another chance, I'd love to eat them again.

58
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:45,000
So, how did you enjoy it? The sounds were wonderful, weren't they?

59
00:26:45,500 --> 00:27:07,000
This treat has been trending in the ASMR community for a while, and kohakuto itself makes very popular crunchy sounds, so I always wanted to try it. Valentine's Day felt like the perfect occasion to enjoy sweets, so I had it today.

60
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:17,000
It was delicious. Did you all have some chocolate today?

61
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:28,000
I did buy chocolate for myself—a slightly fancy one. 5 pieces for 1,000 yen, so 200 yen per piece of luxury chocolate!

62
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:40,500
This Koubutsu Wokashi is also quite a high-end confection, but since there was plenty inside, it was very satisfying.

63
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:54,500
Well then, thank you so much for watching until the end. See you in another video.

64
00:27:56,500 --> 00:28:00,000
Good night.
